{code}
"auth": {
    "type": "BASIC",
    "config": {
      "username": "${APIMAN_AUTH_USERNAME}",
      "password": "${APIMAN_AUTH_PASSWORD}"
    }
  },
{code}

The username required for authentication will actually be "$\{APIMAN_AUTH_USERNAME\}", same for password. No substitution is performed. 

Env variable substitution in this case seems useful when dealing with passwords. Especially for the purpose of docker container this would allow the ability to change the credentials.

