[Configuration File Format|https://apiman.gitbooks.io/apiman-installation-guide/installation-guide/registries-and-components/headless.html#_configuration_file_format] should allow policy configuration to be inlined as native JSON when possible (that is when the policy configuration is actually json.

E.g. instead of 
{code}
"apiPolicies": [{
           "policyJsonConfig": "{ \"responseCode\" : \"403\", \"ipList\" : [ \"1.2.3.4\" ] }", (4)
           "policyImpl": "plugin:io.apiman.plugins:apiman-plugins-url-whitelist-policy:1.3.1.Final:war/io.apiman.gateway.engine.policies.IPWhitelistPolicy" (5)
       }]
{code}

Allow this
{code}
"apiPolicies": [{
           policyConfig: {
                "responseCode": "403",
                "ipList": [ "1.2.3.4"] 
           }
           "policyImpl": "plugin:io.apiman.plugins:apiman-plugins-url-whitelist-policy:1.3.1.Final:war/io.apiman.gateway.engine.policies.IPWhitelistPolicy" (5)
       }]
{code}

This didn't matter much in previous versions of Apiman since the user was unlikely to be writing the  policy configuration manually. However with the introduction of headless gateway the situation has changed.

